From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hermes Studio Local Patches <local-patches@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 14:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(providers): per-provider proxy_url egress and connect
 retry

Lets config.yaml custom providers carry proxy_url (provider editor API,
validation and client UI) and routes coding-agent upstream requests
through it: protocol/proxy-fetch.ts performs the HTTP CONNECT handshake
(optionally over TLS to the proxy itself), tunnels node:http/https/http2
across the socket with ALPN so h2-negotiating edges keep working, and
gateway.ts egresses through it whenever a target carries proxyUrl.

Connection-phase failures (TLS handshake rejection, connect timeouts,
ECONNREFUSED and similar) are retried up to 4 times with linear backoff;
only failures raised before any request byte was written are retried, so
a retry can never duplicate a generation or double-bill.

Also carries the client-side provider editor types and UI for
extra_headers / preserve_client_identity (client companion to the
server-side fields introduced by 0001) plus provider-network-review
tests covering proxyFetch and the gateway.
